# My family in Russian: мой, моя, моё
subtitle: "Say my mum, my dad and my sister in Russian, and see why my has three forms, мой, моя́ and моё, that follow the noun's ending."
thumb: "band \"One word for my? Try three.\" note \"моя́ ма́ма\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Where is it? где, в and на in Russian","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/09-russian-where.cast"}

## My family in Russian: мой, моя́, моё
